    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0450" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg394"/>

                <head>No. 211.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 28, 1876</date>.
                        (Received April 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 395.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit herewith an article and
                    translation thereof from the Daily Federalista, one of the leading newspapers of
                    this city, upon the present commercial and political condition of Mexico. This
                    gloomy and unfavorable view of affairs is quite commonly entertained, especially
                    in commercial circles, throughout the country.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d221-a1.xml" xpointer="d221-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
